        <span data-key="Swap is disk space used when RAM is under pressure; hibernation also needs space to save memory before powering off. The installer sizes a dedicated Swap partition with this in mind. Swap Control checks capacity, the resume target and Swap file offsets. Enough Swap alone does not enable hibernation: hardware and resume settings must also work.">@Localizer["Swap is disk space used when RAM is under pressure; hibernation also needs space to save memory before powering off. The installer sizes a dedicated Swap partition with this in mind. Swap Control checks capacity, the resume target and Swap file offsets. Enough Swap alone does not enable hibernation: hardware and resume settings must also work."]</span>
